  "img": "systems/pf1/icons/skills/yellow_37.jpg",
  "name": "Deadly Performance",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A bard of 20th level or higher can use his performance to cause one enemy to die from joy or sorrow. To be affected, the target must be able to see and hear the bard perform for 1 full round and be within 30 feet. The target receives a Will save (DC 10 + half of the bard's level + his Charisma modifier) to negate the effect. On a success, the target is dazed for 1d4 rounds. On a failure, it dies. Deadly performance is a mind-affecting death effect that relies on audible and visual components.</p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
